  "worked_solution": "To compute the velocity vector, we need to integrate the acceleration vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \u27e83\\sqrt{t},{csc}^{2}\u2061(t)\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e8\\int 3{t}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int {csc}^{2}\u2061(t)\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82{t}^{3/2}+{C}_{1},-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(t)+{C}_{2}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve for the constants of integration using the fact that $v(1)=\u27e84,10\u27e9.$ Substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\u27e82(1)^{3/2}+{C}_{1},-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(1)+{C}_{2}\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e84,10\u27e9 & =\u27e82+{C}_{1},-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(1)+{C}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(1)+{C}_{2} \\\\ {C}_{2} & =10+\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity vector is\n\n$$\nv(t)=\u27e82t\\sqrt{t}+2,\\,-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(t)+10+\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(1)\u27e9.\n$$",
